 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "crystal-osc-10-25mhz",
   "title": "10MHz to 25MHz Crystal Oscillator",
   "page": 1,
   "description": "A crystal oscillator on one 5V rail. R1 and R2, both 2k, set the non-inverting input at mid-supply; R3 and C1 hang a small RC on that node. The crystal runs from Q OUT back to the non-inverting input, while R4 and C2 from Q OUT give the inverting input an averaged copy of the output. The square wave is taken from Q̄ OUT.",
