   "text": "With ±5V supplies the common mode range is –3.75V to 3.5V. In general it reaches from 1.25V above V– to 1.5V below V+, for any supply voltage; the test is that the output still answers a small differential input correctly. One input may go outside the range, as far as the supply, provided the other stays inside. An input taken above the upper limit and then brought back adds up to 10ns of propagation delay; going below the lower limit has no such effect."
  },
  {
