   "page": 8,
   "text": "Without bypass capacitors the supply impedance at the pins lets the rails move with internal currents, and the output oscillates at around 100MHz. Capacitors too far away or lossy still allow oscillation. For linear-region operation the part sits over a ground plane with RF bypass capacitors of 0.01µF or more, leads under 0.2 inch, mounted close to the pins. Sockets are not used."
  },
