   "text": "A miscompensated probe shows false amplitude (an excursion of almost 8V from a 5V part), and a slow or overcompensated probe makes 10ns edges look like 50ns. 1× probes have 20MHz or less of bandwidth and heavy loading and are not used. The probe ground connection is kept to one inch or less; a six-inch ground lead rings."
