   "text": "Figure 16 pairs the part with an LT1122 FET-input integrator. Each output pulse returns a fixed charge (Q = CV) to the summing node, where the input supplies a comparison current; the integrator, with 68pF feedback, sets the pulse rate that balances the input, so output frequency is linear in input voltage. Range is 1Hz to 10MHz for 0V to 10V in, with overrange to 12MHz at VIN = 12V and 140dB (seven decades) of dynamic range. Linearity is 0.03% and full-scale drift 50ppm/°C. An LTC1050 chopper servos the integrator's non-inverting input, so no zero trim is needed; residual zero error is 0.05Hz/°C. Trim: 6.000V in, adjust the 2kΩ pot for 6.000MHz; 10.000V in, trim the 20k resistor for 10.000MHz; repeat until both hold. All ICs are bypassed with 2.2µF on each supply at the pins."
